# REGRESSION FIXTURE (was `todo/t0681`, closed R49 Track A1-IDENTITY).
#
# The `Box[T](x)` CONSTRUCTOR used to ICE on a closure while `Box.new(x)`
# compiled and ran -- two spellings of one operation, one of which panicked:
#
#     Box[Callable[int(int)]] f = Box[Callable[int(int)]]((int n): n * 2)
#     print(f(21))
#         -> rc 101, "GIR module failed validation: call to undefined function @f"
#
#     Box[Callable[int(int)]] f = Box.new((int n): n * 2)
#     print(f(21))
#         -> rc 0, prints 42          <- CORRECT, and the spelling
#                                        docs/book/16-smart-pointers.md teaches
#
# CAUSE: sibling-site drift (Core #4). The `Box.new` path in
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/methods.rs` carried a closure carve-out -- return the
# closure environment struct directly and dispatch through the closure's own
# call body at the call site -- and the `Box[T](...)` constructor arm in
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs` did not, so it boxed the environment and then
# emitted a direct call to a function named after the variable.
#
# The carve-out itself was a `starts_with("__Closure_")` NAME-MATCH, deciding
# semantics from an identifier's spelling, which Layering rule 2 forbids. Both
# arms now ask `TypeMetadata::closure_call_fn` -- CARRIER #1 -- so the typed
# question is asked once and answered the same way in both places.
#
# WHY IT STAYS IN `known_gaps/`: placement only. The self-host lane cannot
# compile the emitted C for this shape yet (`unknown type name
# '__gg_Callable__GorgetClosure'` at `cc`), so it must stay out of the
# auto-scanned `runtime_parity_corpus`. The LIVE test
# `box_ctor_closure_matches_box_new` asserts the output below.
#
# STILL OPEN, and NOT fixed by this: `(*f)` on a `Box[Callable[...]]` is
# rejected with a self-contradicting diagnostic -- `E_DerefNonBox: cannot
# dereference `*` a value of type `Box[Callable[int(int)]]` -- `*` requires a
# `Box[T]`` -- when the value IS a `Box[T]`. Both spellings hit it, so it is
# independent of the ICE. Also still open: the sibling
# `box_callable_call_through_box_undefined_function.gg`, where the payload is a
# `Callable`-typed STRUCT FIELD rather than a closure literal and there is no
# closure environment behind it at all.

void main():
    Box[Callable[int(int)]] f = Box[Callable[int(int)]]((int n): n * 2)
    print(f(21))
